ion_type\\\": \\\"keyboard_enter\\\"}`\\n- Navigate to the home screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_home\\\"}`\\n- Navigate back: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_back\\\"}`\\n- Scroll the screen or a scrollable UI element in one of the four directions, use the same numeric index as above if you want to scroll a specific UI element, leave it empty when scroll the whole screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": <up, down, left, right>, \\\"index\\\": <optional_target_index>}`\\n- Open an app (nothing will happen if the app is not installed): `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"open_app\\\", \\\"app_name\\\": <name>}`\\n- Wait for the screen to update: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"wait\\\"}`\\n\\nThe (overall) user goal/request is:In Simple Calendar Pro, create a calendar event for tomorrow at 16h with the title 'Catch up on Annual Report' and the description 'We will strategize about marketing strategies. Please bring relevant documents.'. The event should last for 60 mins.\\nNow I want you to summerize the latest step based on the action you pick with the reason and descriptions for the before and after (the action) screenshots.\\nHere is the description for the before screenshot:\\nUI element 0: UIElement(text='17', content_description='17 hours', class_name='android.view.View', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=257, x_max=509, y_min=713, y_max=923), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=True, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro', resource_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro:id/material_hour_tv', tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\nUI element 1: UIElement(text='00', content_description='9 minutes', class_name='android.view.View', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=572, x_max=824, y_min=713, y_max=923), hint_text=None, 