 description, start time 16:00, and end time 17:00 for tomorrow. The remaining step is to save the event by tapping the visible Save button.\\nAction: {\\\"action_type\\\":\\\"click\\\",\\\"index\\\":2}\",\n    \"action_prompt\": \"You are an agent who can operate an Android phone on behalf of a user. Based on user's goal/request, you may\\n- Answer back if the request/goal is a question (or a chat message), like user asks \\\"What is my schedule for today?\\\".\\n- Complete some tasks described in the requests/goals by performing actions (step by step) on the phone.\\n\\nWhen given a user request, you will try to complete it step by step. At each step, a list of descriptions for most UI elements on the current screen will be given to you (each element can be specified by an index), together with a history of what you have done in previous steps. Based on these pieces of information and the goal, you must choose to perform one of the action in the following list (action description followed by the JSON format) by outputing the action in the correct JSON format.\\n- If you think the task has been completed, finish the task by using the status action with complete as goal_status: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"goal_status\\\": \\\"complete\\\"}`\\n- If you think the task is not feasible (including cases like you don't have enough information or can not perform some necessary actions), finish by using the `status` action with infeasible as goal_status: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"status\\\", \\\"goal_status\\\": \\\"infeasible\\\"}`\\n- Answer user's question: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"answer\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"<answer_text>\\\"}`\\n- Click/tap on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`.\\n- Long press on a UI element (specified by its index) on the screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"long_press\\\", \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`.\\n- Type text into an editable text field (specified by its index), this action contains clicking the text field, typing in the text and pressing the enter, so no need to click on the target field to start: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": <text_input>, \\\"index\\\": <target_index>}`\\n- Press the Enter key: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"keyboard_enter\\\"}`\\n- Navigate to the home screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_home\\\"}`\\n- Navigate back: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"navigate_back\\\"}`\\n- Scroll the screen or a scrollable UI element in one of the four directions, use the same numeric index as above if you want to scroll a specific UI element, leave it empty when scroll the whole screen: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"direction\\\": <up, down, left, right>, \\\"index\\\": <optional_target_index>}`\\n- Open an app (nothing will happen if the app is not installed): `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"open_app\\\", \\\"app_name\\\": <name>}`\\n- Wait for the screen to update: `{\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"wait\\\"}`\\n\\nThe current user goal/request is: In Simple Calendar Pro, create a calendar event for tomorrow at 16h with the title 'Catch up on Annual Report' and the description 'We will strategize about marketing strategies. Please bring relevant documents.'. The event should last for 60 mins.\\n\\nHere is a history of what you have done so far:\\nStep 1: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"open_app\\\", \\\"app_name\\\": \\\"Simple Calendar Pro\\\"}. Opened Simple Calendar Pro from the home screen successfully; now on the calendar month view (October) with the floating \\u201cNew Event\\u201d button visible, so the next step should be to tap \\u201cNew Event\\u201d to start creating tomorrow\\u2019s 16:00 event.\\nStep 2: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 6}. Tapped the floating New Event button to start creating the calendar item; it worked by expanding the FAB menu and revealing \\u201cEvent\\u201d and \\u201cTask\\u201d options on top of the month view, so next tap \\u201cEvent\\u201d (not Task).\\nStep 3: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 9}. Tapped the visible \\u201cEvent\\u201d option in the expanded FAB menu to start event creation; it worked and opened the \\u201cNew Event\\u201d form with empty Title/Location/Description fields, start date/time preset to tomorrow at 16:00, end time still 16:00, so next fill title/description and adjust end time to 17:00.\\nStep 4: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"Catch up on Annual Report\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Entered the event title into the Title field successfully\\u2014before it showed the placeholder \\u201cTitle,\\u201d and after it shows \\u201cCatch up on Annual Report\\u201d; still need to fill the description and adjust the end time to 17:00 before saving.\\nStep 5: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"input_text\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"We will strategize about marketing strategies. Please bring relevant documents.\\\", \\\"index\\\": 7}. Entered the event description into the Description field (index 7); it worked as expected\\u2014the field now contains \\u201cWe will strategize about marketing strategies. Please bring relevant documents.\\u201d while the event still shows start 16:00 and end 16:00, so next adjust the end time to 17:00 before saving.\\nStep 6: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 11}. Tapped the event end time field (was 16:00 on the New Event form) to adjust the duration; this worked and opened the time picker with hour 16 and minute 00 selected, so next set the end time to 17:00 and confirm with OK.\\nStep 7: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 26}. Tapped hour 17 in the end-time picker to make the event end at 17:00; this worked, as the picker switched from hour selection with 16 selected to minute selection with 17 shown and 00 minutes selected, so next confirm with OK.\\nStep 8: Action selected: {\\\"action_type\\\": \\\"click\\\", \\\"index\\\": 4}. Tapped OK on the time picker to confirm the selected end time; this worked as expected and returned to the New Event form showing start 16:00 and end 17:00, so the event timing is now set correctly and the next step should be saving the event.\\n\\nHere is a list of descriptions for some UI elements on the current screen:\\nUI element 0: UIElement(text=None, content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.ImageButton', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=0, x_max=147, y_min=138, y_max=285), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro', resource_name=None, tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\nUI element 1: UIElement(text='New Event', content_description=None, class_name='android.widget.TextView', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=157, x_max=414, y_min=175, y_max=249), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=False, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=False, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro', resource_name=None, tooltip=None, resource_id=None, metadata=None)\\nUI element 2: UIElement(text=None, content_description='Save', class_name='android.widget.Button', bbox=None, bbox_pixels=BoundingBox(x_min=953, x_max=1080, y_min=148, y_max=274), hint_text=None, is_checked=False, is_checkable=False, is_clickable=True, is_editable=False, is_enabled=True, is_focused=False, is_focusable=True, is_long_clickable=False, is_scrollable=False, is_selected=False, is_visible=True, package_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro', resource_name='com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro:id/save'